  "text": "And because the model is fast and detailed, it lets us do something genuinely new actually optimize the structure. It ranks every wall by how much load it's really carrying, finds the ones doing basically nothing, and demotes them from load-bearing walls to ordinary partitions. It just sweeps through pull out the least-used wall, re-check the building, repeat until everything that's left is genuinely needed. And the rooms never move; the layout, the daylight, the circulation all stay exactly as designed. The only thing that changes is how much timber the building uses. And this works in any design process, by hand or automated not just inside our generator. Which is why, again, we see it as a major outcome on its own.",
